@@ -3,3 +3,12 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+- `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` — JSON Pointer (RFC 6901): returns the referenced value, throws if the
+  pointer is invalid or does not resolve.
+- `applyPatch(document, patch)` — JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
+  `test`. Returns the patched document as a new value; the input document and patch are never mutated or
+  aliased. Throws if the patch is invalid or an operation fails (the patch is then applied not at all).
+  Object members named `__proto__` are treated as ordinary members and never touch the prototype chain.
